     public var listIsBehind = 0.15
+    /// A window that is asked to go somewhere comes to rest where a hosted Mac left it (`Screens.rest`): below the menu bar as well as above the bottom, judged by the display
+    /// that has most of it where its corner's display has a column of it at most, and pulled in sideways where no point of it would be within reach. OFF SO FAR:
+    /// Arbor still reckons by the corner and knows no stop at the top, so that it sends windows out of view to places from which a Mac fetches them into view
+    /// (`WhereAMacLeavesAWindowTests`). It goes on with the change that makes Arbor reckon by the same rule.
